    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required `contactPreference` = `EMAIL` when an email is present, otherwise `PHONE`, on the owner read model (`GET /api/owners/{id}`, which the acceptance tests exercise after `POST /api/owners`).\n\nTwo changes, following the project's existing derived-field pattern (like `locality`, `membershipNumber`, `bulkSignupWarning`):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema, so `OwnerDto` gains the field on code generation.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` that derives it via a new `contactPreference(owner)` helper: returns `\"EMAIL\"` when `owner.getEmail()` is non-null and non-blank, otherwise `\"PHONE\"`.\n\nBoth acceptance tests (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) and the full suite pass: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
